        "comments": "The assembly fCobTae1.hap1.1 is based on 39x Oxford Nanopore data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project (https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial Oxford Nanopore assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Order and orientation of scaffolds on chromosome 1 from\n42.65-45.36Mb, chromosome 3 from\n20.67-38.95Mb, chromosome 4 from\n33.53-41.29Mb, chromosome 5 from\n23.01-49.63Mb, chromosome 6 from\n23.80-25.31Mb, chromosome 7 from\n19.99-26.50Mb, chromosome 10 from\n29.11-39.58Mb, chromosome 13 from\n11.30-12.81Mb, and chromosome 14 from\n2.91-4.32Mb is unsure.",
